[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Parry Loot[/b] is a lightweight, vanilla-friendly ModEngine 2 DLL mod that grants a short [b]Item Discovery[/b] boost whenever [b]you[/b] land a successful parry, lasting long enough to still be active when your riposte kills the enemy.

By default, every clean parry grants [b]+25 Item Discovery for 15 seconds[/b] (half the strength of a Silver-Pickled Fowl Foot). Because it works purely through runtime hooks and touches [b]zero[/b] [i]regulation.bin[/i] parameters or talisman slots, it plays nicely with overhauls, randomizers, weapon mods, and custom parameter merges.

Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/ParryLoot]github.com/Lumpish-Haggard/ParryLoot[/url][/color][/size]

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Vortex:[/b] click [i]Mod Manager Download[/i], then enable the mod and deploy. Vortex's Elden Ring support sets up ModEngine 2 itself and writes [i]"mods\\ParryLoot.dll"[/i] into [i]config_eldenring.toml[/i] on every deploy, so skip to the last step.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Manual:[/b] install [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2]ModEngine 2[/url] if you have not already, then extract the [i]mods[/i] folder into your ModEngine 2 folder (next to [i]modengine2_launcher.exe[/i] and [i]config_eldenring.toml[/i]; the Elden Ring [i]Game[/i] folder if you installed ModEngine 2 there).[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Manual:[/b] open [i]config_eldenring.toml[/i] and add [i]"mods\\ParryLoot.dll"[/i] inside [i]external_dlls = [ ... ][/i].[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Launch via ModEngine 2 (offline / non-EAC only). The mod writes [i]mods\ParryLoot.log[/i] next to [i]ParryLoot.dll[/i] each time the game starts.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]No regulation.bin edits:[/b] Compatible with virtually any mod setup (vanilla, Reforged, Convergence, Randomizer, custom [i]regulation.bin[/i] merges) and safe to add or remove anytime.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]No talisman needed:[/b] Triggers purely on your parry timing, with no equipment slot tax.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]All parry types supported:[/b] Triggers on melee parries (Parry on any shield or weapon that has it, Buckler Parry, Golden Parry, Storm Wall, Carian Retaliation melee) and spell/projectile parries (Carian Retaliation, Thops's Barrier).[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Zero false positives:[/b] Ignores normal blocks, Guard Counters, i-frame rolls, whiffed parries, partial guard-breaks, and enemies parrying you.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]ERBuffTimer support:[/b] Applies vanilla SpEffect 3970 with a finite 15s duration so ERBuffTimer displays the countdown icon automatically.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Respects real Silver-Pickled Fowl Feet:[/b] Never shortens or reduces a real 180s (+50) Silver-Pickled Fowl Foot if one is active.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Stacks with Arcane cap & Silver Scarab:[/b] Adds directly on top of the 99 Arcane (199 discovery) cap, Arcane-boosting gear, and Silver Scarab (+75).[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]INI configurable:[/b] Customize [i]item_discovery_bonus[/i], [i]duration[/i], melee/spell toggles, and logging in [i]mods\ParryLoot.ini[/i].[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2]ModEngine 2[/url]: [b]required[/b] (or another external DLL loader).[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]ERBuffTimer: optional, to see the live countdown icon on screen.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Elden Ring App Ver. 1.17.2+ (uses AOB pattern scanning).[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]FAQ[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Do I need to equip a specific talisman?[/b]
No. It triggers directly on your successful parries without requiring Assassin's Crimson Dagger or any talisman slot.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Why is this a DLL mod instead of a regulation.bin edit?[/b]
Modifying [i]regulation.bin[/i] conflicts with overhauls, randomizers, and weapon/rule mods unless manually merged in Smithbox. Because Parry Loot hooks parry resolution in memory via AOB signatures, it touches [b]zero[/b] game parameter files and can be added or removed safely anytime.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Why +25 Item Discovery for 15 seconds?[/b]
Enemies don't drop loot on the parry itself: you follow up with a riposte. A 15-second duration keeps the bonus active until the riposte kills your opponent, while +25 stays vanilla-friendly (half a Silver-Pickled Fowl Foot's +50). You can customize both in [i]mods\ParryLoot.ini[/i].[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Which parries work, and can blocks, Guard Counters, rolls, or whiffed parries trigger it?[/b]
Triggers on melee weapon/shield parries (Parry on any shield or weapon that has it, Buckler Parry, Golden Parry, Storm Wall, Carian Retaliation melee) and spell/projectile parries (Carian Retaliation, Thops's Barrier). Ignores normal blocks, Guard Counters, i-frame rolls, whiffed parries, partial guard-breaks, and an enemy parrying you.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Does ERBuffTimer display the buff timer icon?[/b]
Yes. Parry Loot applies vanilla SpEffect 3970 with finite remaining and total duration (15.0s), so ERBuffTimer displays the Silver-Pickled Fowl Foot icon and countdown automatically.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Does it stack with Silver Scarab and Arcane gear?[/b]
Yes, additively. Elden Ring sums all active Item Discovery SpEffects, so Silver Scarab (+75) stacks with Parry Loot (+25 = +100 total), and Arcane-boosting gear (Silver Tear Mask, Marika's Scarseal/Soreseal, Godrick's Great Rune, Outer God Heirloom) scales your base Arcane underneath it.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Does it still work past the 99 Arcane hard cap?[/b]
Yes. Elden Ring's [i]GetItemDiscovery[/i] caps the Arcane stat curve at 99 Arcane (199 base Discovery), then adds all SpEffect Item Discovery bonuses afterward with [b]no upper limit[/b]. At 99 Arcane, Parry Loot still adds +25 (224 total, or 299 with Silver Scarab).[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Does it stack with a Silver-Pickled Fowl Foot consumable?[/b]
No, by design. Both share SpEffect 3970 so ERBuffTimer renders its vanilla icon cleanly. If a real 180s (+50) Silver-Pickled Fowl Foot is active, Parry Loot leaves it untouched without shortening or weakening it; eating a real Fowl Foot during Parry Loot's 15s window immediately upgrades you to the full 180s at +50.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Can I customize the values or use this online?[/b]
You can tune bonus amount, duration, melee/spell triggers, and logging in [i]mods\ParryLoot.ini[/i]. Like all ModEngine 2 DLL mods, play offline with EAC disabled.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]My parries do nothing. What should I check?[/b]
[i]mods\ParryLoot.log[/i] next to [i]ParryLoot.dll[/i]. If it was not written when the game started, ModEngine 2 did not load the DLL: [i]config_eldenring.toml[/i] must list [i]"mods\\ParryLoot.dll"[/i] in [i]external_dlls[/i]. Vortex rewrites that list on every deploy from the mods it installed, so with Vortex install the mod through Vortex rather than copying the files by hand. If the log has an ERROR or WARNING line, please post it in the Bugs tab.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]

